      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ be bases of ${R}^{2}.$ \nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ from $B$ to $C$ given that\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $C.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
